# Tests — structural audit infrastructure only
tests/rubrics/principles.md
tests/commands/session/spec.md
tests/scripts/*.py

# Data — standard D&D reference catalogs
# NOTE: spell/monster bodies are copied wholesale. Keep their commentary campaign-neutral
# in the source repo before syncing — do not let campaign proper nouns (NPC names, place
# names, module names) leak into these reference files, or they ship into the template.
data/backgrounds/*.md
data/classes/*.md
data/deities/*.md
data/feats/*.md
data/monsters/*.md
data/races/*.md
data/resources/*.md
data/skills/*.md
data/spells/*.md

# Exclusions — world-specific resources inside data/resources/
# These are homebrew or world-economy entries that belong to this campaign, not the engine.
# A new campaign should create its own world resources from scratch.
# Add a line here whenever a new world-specific resource lands in data/resources/.
#!data/resources/Example.md        # example: a player-contributed, world-specific resource to exclude

# Scripts — all engine scripts and shared library (globs, so new scripts ship without an edit here)
scripts/*.py
scripts/*.ps1
scripts/lib/*.py
# Orphaned: superseded by scripts/fetch-maps.py, referenced by nothing
!scripts/inkarnate-fetch.py
!scripts/test_inkarnate_fetch.py

# Charting app — timeline/swimlane chart engine (TS + Vite)
# Whole tree is shareable engine infrastructure (components, helpers, specs,
# build config, lockfile). Demo page is template-only debugging scaffolding.
app/**
!app/pages/demo/**

# IDE / graph config
.vscode/settings.json
.vscode/extensions.json
